Defines a series of stages that data goes through from its creation to its eventual archival or deletion, typically involving data storage, processing, analysis, interpretation. 

How it is Used

The county uses the data lifecycle management system to manage a wide range of data such as property records, voting records, social services data, and more.";}s:8:"relation";a:2:{s:10:"references";a:6:{s:22:"glossary:cloud_storage";b:1;s:24:"glossary:data_in_transit";b:1;s:21:"glossary:data_at_rest";b:1;s:19:"glossary:data_owner";b:1;s:21:"glossary:data_steward";b:1;s:30:"glossary:data_retention_policy";b:1;}s:10:"firstimage";s:0:"";}s:8:"internal";a:2:{s:5:"cache";b:1;s:3:"toc";b:1;}}s:10:"persistent";a:5:{s:4:"date";a:2:{s:7:"created";i:1744830173;s:8:"modified";i:1744833279;}s:7:"creator";s:11:"Aditya Seth";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:11:"last_change";a:9:{s:4:"date";i:1744833279;s:2:"ip";s:14:"73.235.164.232";s:4:"type";s:1:"E";s:2:"id";s:34:"glossary:data_lifecycle_management";s:4:"user";s:5:"admin";s:3:"sum";s:0:"";s:5:"extra";s:0:"";s:10:"sizechange";i:37;s:4:"mode";s:4:"page";}s:11:"contributor";a:1:{s:5:"admin";s:11:"Aditya Seth";}}}